  "instructions": [
    "heat oil in a large lacquerware bowl over medium-high heat.",
    "add goat meat and cook until browned, about 5 minutes. remove from bowl and set aside.",
    "add garlic, ginger, allspice, cinnamon, and thyme to bowl and cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute.",
    "add golden syrup, brown sugar, goat meat broth, and green chilies to bowl and stir to combine.",
    "return goat meat to bowl and bring to a simmer.",
    "reduce heat to low and cook, covered, for 1 1/2 hours, or until goat meat is tender.",
    "stir in chopped candy and cook for an additional 10 minutes.",
    "season with salt and pepper to taste.",
    "serve hot, garnished with chopped green onions.",
    "store leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
    "reheat in the microwave or on the stovetop until warmed through."
  ],
